  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of NNN integers.\n\nYou perform the following operation on it N−1N - 1N−1 times:\n\n\nChoose index iii (1≤i&lt;∣A∣1 \\le i &lt; |A|1≤i&lt;∣A∣) and let X=Ai+2⋅Ai+1X = A_i + 2 \\cdot A_{i + 1}X=Ai​+2⋅Ai+1​.\nDelete AiA_iAi​ and Ai+1A_{i + 1}Ai+1​ from the array AAA.\nInsert XXX back to the array AAA in the same place.\nMore formally, you replace array AAA with A[1,i−1]+[X]+A[i+2,N]A[1, i - 1] + [X] + A[i + 2, N]A[1,i−1]+[X]+A[i+2,N], where A[L,R]A[L, R]A[L,R] represents the subarray [AL,AL+1,…,AR][A_L, A_{L + 1}, \\ldots, A_R][AL​,AL+1​,…,AR​].\n\nAt the end of the N−1N - 1N−1 operations, only one element remains. What is the minimum and maximum possible value of that last element?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN - the size of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum and maximum possible value of the final element.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "2≤N≤202 \\le N \\le 202≤N≤20",
      "1≤Ai≤1001 \\le A_i \\le 1001≤Ai​≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
